# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# This is not tidiness. The shared match configuration must be byte-identical
# on both peers (M#11), and the pre-match handshake compares its SHA-256. If one
# team's machine checks the file out with CRLF and the other's with LF, the two
# digests differ and the match is refused before the first move. Pinning LF
# removes that entire class of failure — and silences Git's CRLF warnings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose bytes must never be rewritten.
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Binary assets: leave alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
